 "method": "Heather final integration (2026-11-02): LOUDNESS QUALITY GATE, read-only. Run before apply.py.\n\nThe founder chose the six takes from a level-matched comparison, so their real production levels\nwere not part of that decision. Each take is measured here as it would ship (the frozen rule:\nHeather's frozen median and voice gain, no extra gain), against Heather's pack as it ships today\n(43 clips, including the three seed-32 files integrated earlier on 2026-11-02).\n\nPer take:\n  - integrated / max momentary / max short-term loudness, speech p90, true peak;\n  - the frozen rule's own record (raw level, outlier correction into the +/-2 LU window, limiter);\n  - jump against its own shipping original, against Heather's part median, and against the\n    clips that play next to a part in a session (the leads \"First.\" / \"Next.\" / \"Last.\" and the\n    ending), by speech p90 (the level of the spoken words, comparable for one-word leads);\n  - the 2026-10-17 level-correction formula: extra gain = -mean excess of I, M_max and S_max over\n    Heather's part median.\nObjective trim criteria, fixed before measuring (a static gain by the 2026-10-17 route only):\n  T1  the take breaks the frozen standard: true peak above the limiter ceiling, or the rule had\n      to limit it;\n  T2  it would be a new loudness extreme: louder than every Heather part now shipping on I, M_max\n      or S_max (a level the founder has not heard from Heather in the app);\n  T3  its 2026-10-17 correction is at least the smallest one the founder has confirmed by ear as\n      needed (getItOut, -1.8 dB; heard \"too loud\", 2026-10-17).\nWrites only heather_final_integration_2026-11-02/loudness_gate.json.\nUsage: python -I loudness_gate.py <repo>\n",
